    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d431">

                <pb facs="0528" n="518" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg518"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.0023/3–3147: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the Soviet
                        Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Smith</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-05-10T15:00:00-04:00">May 10, 1947—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1151. As Emb is aware Dept knows no feasible means conduct courier service Dairen
                    other than that to which FonOff will so far not accede. (Urtel 1102 Mar 31, 11
                    a.m. and Nanking’s 945, May 2 to Dept.<anchor n="73" xml:id="d431-f1"/>) We had
                    hoped that transfer control Dairen to Chinese Govt would solve problem but there
                    seems to be little promise of early transfer. Accordingly suggest you discuss
                    courier problem with FonOff with view (Sent Moscow repeated Nanking) persuading
                    Soviets reconsider attitude or exploring other feasible possibilities.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d431-f1" n="73" xml:id="d431-f1-content">
                <p>Latter not printed; it reported that 10 bags of classified mail and 6 sea pouches
                    had accumulated at Shanghai for Dairen (051.93/5–247).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
